<Base title="Tools" description="Interactive tools by Abhay Tewari: a W-GAN + EVT catastrophe reinsurance pricing lab, a business-cycle investing compass and the ZENOJAS XGBoost stock-selection model.">
  <div class="article-head"><div class="eyebrow">Tools</div><h1>Working models you can run</h1><p class="lede">Everything below runs in your browser on public data. They are research prototypes, published so that the methods can be examined, not products or advice.</p></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card tool"><div class="meta"><span>Reinsurance · Generative AI · EVT</span></div><h3><a href="/tools/pricing-lab/">Catastrophe pricing lab (W-GAN + EVT)</a></h3><p>The Gift Re Pricing Lab: catastrophe excess-of-loss pricing for Indian flood, cyclone, earthquake and drought. Conditional WGAN-GP scenarios, GPD tail splice, compound-Poisson simulation, RBC capital and technical premium, compared against lognormal and empirical benchmarks. The W-GAN models were trained with AI assistance (Claude) and are documented in the <a href="/blog/pricing-catastrophes-with-wgan-and-evt/">blog post on the method</a>.</p><p><a class="btn" href="/tools/pricing-lab/">Open the lab</a> &nbsp; <a href="/blog/pricing-catastrophes-with-wgan-and-evt/">Read how it works</a></p></article>
    <article class="card tool"><div class="meta"><span>Investing · Business cycle · NSE ETFs</span></div><h3><a href="/tools/cycle-compass/">Cycle Compass</a></h3><p>Score the indicator chain for India and the US, get a phase reading (early recovery, mid expansion, late cycle, contraction) with a confidence multiplier, and see the sector tilts, ETF menu and deployment rules for that phase.</p><p><a class="btn" href="/tools/cycle-compass/">Open the compass</a> &nbsp; <a href="/blog/reading-the-business-cycle/">Read the playbook</a></p></article>
    <article class="card tool"><div class="meta"><span>Investing · Machine learning · NSE</span></div><h3><a href="/tools/zenojas/">ZENOJAS Stock Model</a></h3><p>A shallow, regularised XGBoost model (now the first-choice ranker, replacing the earlier BiLSTM) scores ~940 NSE stocks each quarter on the probability of a top-200 return; the 30 highest form an equal-weight portfolio. A 21-quarter out-of-sample backtest you can re-cut over any window, in-sample vs out-of-sample and net-of-cost checks, and candid caveats on selection bias, size tilt and costs.</p><p><a class="btn" href="/tools/zenojas/">Open the model</a> &nbsp; <a href="/tools/zenojas/explorer/">Backtest Explorer</a> &nbsp; <a href="/tools/zenojas/picks/">Predicted stocks</a> &nbsp; <a href="/tools/zenojas/how-it-works/">How it works</a></p></article>
  </div>
</Base>
